There are two isomers with the formula $\text{Ni}(\text{R}_3\text{P})_2\text{I}_2$, but only one structure with the formula $\text{Co}(\text{R}_3\text{P})_2\text{I}_2$. ($R = \text{alkyl}$, $\text{R}_3\text{P}$ is a monodentate ligand)

Draw diagrams showing the structure of $\text{Co}(\text{R}_3\text{P})_2\text{I}_2$ and the two isomers of $\text{Ni}(\text{R}_3\text{P})_2\text{I}_2$.

